# UI and shadcn

The UI uses shadcn on Radix with Tailwind 4. The admin portal copies the look of the Driving-Test admin users page. `docs/PLAN.md` section 5 has the full spec.

## 1. shadcn components

Must:
- Add components with the CLI (`npx shadcn@latest add <name>`), so they land in `src/components/ui/`.
- Check `src/components/ui/` before adding anything. Use what exists.
- Build feature components by composing `ui/` components in `src/components/<feature>/`.
- Use `asChild` to render a shadcn component as another element (`<Button asChild><Link href={...} /></Button>`).
- Use variants (`variant`, `size`) for styling differences. Add a new variant inside the `ui/` component's `cva` config when several features need it.
- Use the right component for each job.

| Need | Component |
|---|---|
| Confirming a destructive action | `AlertDialog` |
| A form or details in a modal | `Dialog` on desktop, `Drawer` or `Sheet` on mobile when the content is tall |
| Feedback after an action | `toast` from `sonner` |
| A form field with label, description and error | `Field`, `FieldLabel`, `FieldDescription`, `FieldError` |
| Options in a filter | `Select`, or `Combobox` (Popover with Command) when there are more than about 10 |
| A row menu with more than three actions | `DropdownMenu` |
| An icon-only button | `Button size="icon"` with a `Tooltip` and an `aria-label` |
| Status labels | `Badge` |
| Loading placeholders | `Skeleton` |
| Empty results | `Empty` |

Never:
- Hand-write a component that shadcn provides (buttons, dialogs, selects, tooltips, tables).
- Edit a `ui/` component for one feature's needs. Pass `className` or compose a wrapper.
- Use raw Radix packages directly in feature code. Go through `ui/`.
- Mix in another component library.
- Use an icon set other than `lucide-react`.

## 2. Theme and styling

Must:
- Use semantic color tokens (`bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-destructive`). Define new colors as CSS variables in `globals.css` for both light and dark mode, then register them in the `@theme` block.
- Use `cn()` to merge class names.
- Check every screen in light and dark mode.

Never:
- Use hex values, `rgb()` or Tailwind palette colors (`bg-green-600`, `text-gray-500`) in components. Add a token instead, such as `--success`.
- Use inline `style` for anything Tailwind can express.

## 3. Admin portal shell

The boilerplate ships the shell in `src/components/admin/`. It combines a sidebar for the main tabs with a top navbar for the account controls. It follows the shadcn `sidebar-07` block, which collapses to icons.

Must:
- Add admin pages under `src/app/(admin)/admin/` so they get the shell from `(admin)/admin/layout.tsx`.
- Add sidebar links to the `ADMIN_NAV` constant, with an icon, a label from copy constants and a route from `ROUTES`. Group them under labels such as "Main". Use a collapsible item for sub-pages.
- Keep the navbar to the sidebar trigger on the left, and the theme toggle and user menu on the right.
- Start every admin page with `PageHeader` (title and description), then optional KPI cards, then the main content.
- Keep the layout a server component. The sidebar, trigger, theme toggle and user menu are the client components.

When a new project needs another portal:
- For a sidebar portal, copy the `(admin)` layout and the `components/admin/` shell, and give it its own nav constant. If you need a fresh copy of the template, run `npx shadcn@latest add sidebar-07`, move the generated files into `components/<portal>/` and delete the demo parts (team switcher, projects list, sample data).
- For a navbar-only portal, compose the marketing navbar pattern: `NavigationMenu` for desktop links, `Sheet` for the mobile menu and `DropdownMenu` for the avatar menu.

Never:
- Install `dashboard-01` or another full-page block into the project. They bring demo data and charts. Copy only the parts you need.
- Build a second sidebar implementation.

## 4. Tables

Every table that lists records follows the users table in `src/components/users/`. The feature list below is required.

Must:
- Build tables from `src/components/data-table/`: `DataTable`, `TableToolbar`, `SortableHead`, `DataTablePagination`, `DataTableLoadMore` and `TableRefreshButton`.
- Paginate on the server, with the control that matches the endpoint's strategy (`backend-database.mdc` section 6).
  - For offset endpoints, use `DataTablePagination`. It has first, previous, page numbers with ellipsis, next and last buttons, a "showing X to Y of Z" label and a rows-per-page select using `PAGE_SIZE_OPTIONS`. The users table is the example.
  - For cursor endpoints, use `DataTableLoadMore` with `useInfiniteQuery`. It shows a "Load more" `LoadingButton` while `hasMore` is true, and a "No more results" note after the last page. The audit log table is the example.
- Give each table a search input with a search icon, debounced with `useDebouncedValue` (350 ms by default), and send it to the backend `search` param.
- Give each table filters for its main enum and date fields, using `Select` with an "All" option.
- Make sortable columns cycle through ascending, descending and off on click.
- Keep search, filters, sort, page and page size in the URL through `useTableUrlState`. Changing any of them except the page resets the page to 1. Cursor tables keep search, filters and sort in the URL but not the cursor, and a filter change starts the list over.
- Show one `Skeleton` row per row in the page while loading, an error row with the message on failure, and an `Empty` row when nothing matches.
- Dim the table while a background refetch runs (`isFetching && !isLoading`).
- Hide lower-priority columns on small screens with `hidden md:table-cell` or `hidden lg:table-cell`. Name and actions stay visible.
- Make row actions icon buttons with a `Tooltip` and an `aria-label`. Destructive actions open an `AlertDialog`.
- Match the styling: a `rounded-xl` bordered card, a dark primary header row, alternating row backgrounds and a filled primary Refresh button on the right of the toolbar.

Never:
- Fetch every row and paginate, filter or sort in the browser.
- Fire a request on every keystroke.
- Build a table as one large component. Split it into toolbar, columns, row actions and dialogs.
- Copy `useDebouncedValue` or pagination math into a feature file.

## 5. Forms

Forms use React Hook Form, Zod and a React Query mutation.

Must:
- Define the schema in `src/schemas/<feature>.ts`, with the same length limits as the backend DTO. Infer the form type with `z.infer`.
- Use `zodResolver(schema)` and render fields with `Field`, `FieldLabel`, `FieldError` and the matching `ui/` input.
- Show an error under each invalid field, and connect it with `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby`. `Field` handles both.
- Map backend `400` field errors onto the form with `setError`, using the `mapApiFieldErrors` helper.
- Show form-level errors, such as "Invalid email or password", in `FormErrorAlert` above the submit button.
- Submit with `mutation.mutate` and show success with a toast or a redirect.
- Give inputs the right `type`, `autoComplete` and `inputMode` (`email`, `current-password`, `new-password`, `one-time-code`).
- Use `PasswordInput` for passwords. It has a show and hide toggle.

Never:
- Validate only on the backend or only on the frontend.
- Clear the form when a submission fails.
- Show raw error objects or status codes to the user.

## 6. Loading states on buttons

Must:
- Use `LoadingButton` for every button that starts a request: form submits, confirm buttons in dialogs, row actions and refresh.
- Pass the pending state (`loading={mutation.isPending}`). The button disables itself, shows a spinner and keeps its width.
- Disable the dialog's cancel and close controls while its confirm action is pending.

Never:
- Leave a request button clickable while its request is in flight.
- Replace the button label with a spinner only. Keep the label and add the spinner beside it.

## 7. Responsive layout

Must:
- Write mobile styles first and add `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` and `xl:` overrides.
- Check every screen at 375 px, 768 px and 1280 px.
- Make touch targets at least 40 px tall on mobile.
- Stack toolbars vertically on mobile (`flex-col gap-3 lg:flex-row`).
- Scroll wide tables horizontally inside their card, never the whole page.

Never:
- Use fixed pixel widths on containers. Use `max-w-*` and `w-full`.

## 8. Accessibility

Must:
- Give every input a visible label or an `aria-label` from copy constants.
- Give icon-only buttons an `aria-label`, and mark decorative icons `aria-hidden`.
- Keep keyboard focus visible. shadcn's focus ring is the default, so don't remove it.
- Use semantic elements: `button` for actions, `a` or `Link` for navigation, and one `h1` per page.
- Show status with text or an icon as well as color.

## Review checklist

- [ ] Components come from `ui/` through the shadcn CLI. No hand-built replacements and no feature edits to `ui/`.
- [ ] Colors use semantic tokens. No hex values or palette classes.
- [ ] Admin pages sit under `(admin)/admin/`, start with `PageHeader` and are linked in `ADMIN_NAV`.
- [ ] Every table has server pagination with the control matching its strategy, plus debounced search, filters, sorting and URL state.
- [ ] Tables show skeleton, error and empty rows, and hide low-priority columns on small screens.
- [ ] Forms use Zod schemas, `Field` errors, backend error mapping and `FormErrorAlert`.
- [ ] Every request button is a `LoadingButton` with its pending state wired.
- [ ] Screens work at 375, 768 and 1280 px in light and dark mode.
- [ ] Icon buttons have `aria-label` and a tooltip. Inputs have labels.
